WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.002 --> 00:00:07.120
"Don’t Eat Raw Alfalfa Sprouts"

00:00:07.266 --> 00:00:08.560
According to the U.S. Centers

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.160
for Disease Control
and Prevention,

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.320
we should cook alfalfa sprouts,

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.600
because eating raw sprouts

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.600
can lead to salmonella
food poisoning.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.760
It's especially important
not to eat raw sprouts

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.520
if you are particularly old
or young,

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.360
immunosuppressed, or pregnant.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.920
How serious of an issue
is this?

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.960
Over the last few decades,
at least 2,700 Americans

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.560
have been sickened by sprouts.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.040
That's more than
a hundred people a year.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.400
Of course,
during that same time,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.560
more than a hundred thousand
Americans

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.400
were being food poisoned
by eggs

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.680
contaminated with Salmonella.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.120
Indeed, Salmonella in eggs
is a national epidemic

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.160
in the United States.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.200
Salmonella is a gift
that can keep on giving,

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.600
triggering arthritis sometimes,

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.080
which, in rare cases,
can last a lifetime.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:53.120
So, no sprouts
on that sandwich,

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.840
but do you hear the CDC
saying no eggs,

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:58.880
even though they cause
a thousand times more illness?

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:03.040
No, but the CDC does say
no raw or runny eggs,

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.000
no soft-boiled eggs,
no sunny side up.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.440
Even the egg industry itself
admits that over-easy,

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.680
poached, sunny side up,
or soft-boiled eggs

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.560
can't be considered safe.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.080
No wonder eggs are sickening
100,000 Americans a year.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:21.680
Eggs have to be cooked hard
to kill off their bacteria.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.680
Similarly, if we boiled
our sprouts,

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:24.880
they would be safe, too,

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.040
but no one wants
to do that either.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:30.480
The largest national sampling
was from about a decade ago,

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.560
when the Food and Drug
Administration tested sprouts

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:33.520
and sprout facilities

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.680
from all over
the United States.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.280
The agency found that 1 percent
of alfalfa sprout samples

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.360
were affected, and even worse,

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.960
ten percent of alfalfa sprout
seed samples were, too.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.040
So, that's why you can't
just grow them yourself.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.960
The bacteria can get
into the nooks and crannies

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.800
of the alfalfa seed itself.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.480
The majority of outbreaks
have been linked to alfalfa,

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.600
but there' also been outbreaks
tied to clover sprouts,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.560
mung bean sprouts

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.320
(which are more like
typical bean sprouts),

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.640
and sprouted chia.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.480
The national FDA survey
did not find any salmonella

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.080
in mung bean sprouts,
but did find

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.520
that about two percent
were contaminated

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:10.640
with Listeria,

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.800
which can be a particularly
devastating infection

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.640
for pregnant women.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.240
What about the deadly
Jack in the Box

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:19.520
E. coli O157:H7?

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.720
How often can it be found
in retail ground beef,

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.640
sprouts, and mushrooms?

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.960
Well, none were found
in any mushrooms,

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.080
but 1 out of every 90
or so samples of burger meat

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.040
was contaminated,

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.760
and about 1 out of just 70
sprout containers.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.640
But what if you really like
raw sprouts?

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.000
Instead of alfalfa,
use broccoli sprouts.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.760
They have smooth seeds,

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.280
and after testing
the equivalent

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:46.960
of about five million packages,

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.280
less than one in a thousand
bulk samples

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:50.320
turned up positive

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.080
and that may have been
contamination

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.000
from other types of sprouts.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.840
Broccoli sprouts
are easy and cheap

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.240
to make on your own
kitchen counter,

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.560
like I do
for pennies a serving.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.000
I have more than a dozen videos

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.920
on all the amazing things
the sulforaphane

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:05.120
in broccoli sprouts can do,

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.000
everything from treating
autism spectrum disorder

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.280
to detoxifying the effects
of air pollution.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.560
They've also been shown
to combat

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.080
different types
of cancer cells.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:15.440
And you can pretty much
only get

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.920
this natural
immune system enhancer

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.560
in cruciferous vegetables
like broccoli,

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:21.360
broccoli sprouts,

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.440
and I guess
if you're really desperate,

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.703
broccoli beer.

